<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Supplement to Design of TermiBench</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix A Supplement to Design of TermiBench ‣ Shell or Nothing: Real-World Benchmarks and Memory-Activated Agents for Automated Penetration Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> presents the 30 CVEs incorporated in TermiBench along with the 25 services they affect, spanning the years 2015 to 2025. In addition, the 14 selected benign mainstream services are listed in the Table <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix A Supplement to Design of TermiBench ‣ Shell or Nothing: Real-World Benchmarks and Memory-Activated Agents for Automated Penetration Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. By combining these vulnerable services with varying numbers of benign services, we ultimately constructed the 510 target machines in TermiBench.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:50%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8. </span>14 benign services used in TermiBench.</figcaption>
